<title>USA: Bradlees Q4 shr loss $5.19 vs loss $9.54.</title>
<headline>Bradlees Q4 shr loss $5.19 vs loss $9.54.</headline>
<dateline>BRAINTREE, Mass. 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>BRADLEES, INC.</p>
<p>			(Operating as Debtor-In-Possession)</p>
<p>		     CONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF OPERATIONS</p>
<p>		(Dollars in thousands except per share amounts)</p>
<p>			    13 Wks     14 Wks     52 Wks     53 Wks</p>
<p>			     Ended     Ended	Ended	Ended</p>
<p>			   Feb. 1     Feb. 3,    Feb. 1,    Feb. 3,</p>
<p>				1997	1996	 1997	 1996</p>
<p> Net sales	     449,981    575,603  1,561,718  1,780,768</p>
<p> Cost of goods sold  332,885    423,558  1,127,651  1,289,077</p>
<p>  Gross margin	  117,096    152,015    434,067    491,691</p>
<p>Loss before interest, asset</p>
<p>impairment charges, reorganization</p>
<p>items and income taxes</p>
<p>			   (1,802)   (13,605)   (98,020)  (122,307)</p>
<p>Loss before income taxes</p>
<p>			  (59,155)  (162,632)  (218,759)  (311,946)</p>
<p> Income tax benefit	---     53,766	  ---    104,533</p>
<p> Net Loss	    ( 59,155) ( 108,866) ( 218,759) ( 207,413)</p>
<p>Net loss per share:</p>
<p>			   ( 5.19)    ( 9.54)   ( 19.17)   ( 18.17)</p>
<p>NOTE: Bradlees recorded a non-cash charge of $40.8 million in Q4 1996, $99.4 million in all of 1996, reflecting an accouting for the impairment of long-lived assets and for long-lived assets to be disposed.</p>
<p>NOTE: The company said it has received a one-year extension of its $200 million debtor-in-posession financing, subject to approval by the U.S. Bankruptcy Court.</p>
</text>
